{"condensed":"Documentation guide for deploying and building sbc-auth API and Web/UI components to OpenShift namespaces (dev, tools).

Operator authenticates via `oc login`, switches namespace context with `oc project` (dev for deployments, tools for builds), then processes templates with `oc process` using component-specific JSON templates and parameters (NAME, TAG_NAME, REPLICAS, GIT_REF, JENKINS_FILE), applying results with `oc apply`. For API: deploys postgresql database, creates ConfigMap and Secrets via auth-api-pre-deploy.json, creates DeploymentConfig/Service/Route via auth-api-deploy.json, builds via auth-api-build.json, creates pipeline via auth-api-pipeline.json. For Web/UI: creates ConfigMap/Secrets via auth-web-pre-deploy.json, creates DeploymentConfig/Service/Route via auth-web-deploy.json, builds Web via auth-web-build.json and runtime via auth-web-runtime-build.json, creates pipeline via auth-web-pipeline.json. Operator manually updates Secret values in Web Console after creation. Pipeline parameter WEBHOOK routes to GitHub (bcgov/sbc-auth.git); JAEGER_COLLECTOR routes to jaeger-collector service; JENKINS_FILE references ./jenkins/dev.groovy. No entry-point checks shown. Objects queried and deleted by label (app=auth-api, app-group=sbc-auth, template=auth-api-deploy).

GOTCHA: Guide warns "Don't put the real secret inside the template file" but shows no enforcement—secrets require manual Web Console replacement. GOTCHA: PVC deletion marked "(Danger!!)" when deleting by label but no guard prevents accidental deletion. GOTCHA: Guide states it will move to LEAR Documentation but is currently here.","references":[{"target":"OpenShift CLI (oc)","relation":"Commands authenticate to OpenShift, switch namespaces, process templates into manifests, apply manifests to create/update resources, and query/delete resources by label."},{"target":"GitHub (https://github.com/bcgov/sbc-auth.git)","relation":"GIT_REPO_URL and GIT_REF parameters specify the repository and branch that build configs clone and build from."},{"target":"Jenkins (./jenkins/dev.groovy)","relation":"JENKINS_FILE parameter specifies the Groovy pipeline definition that the pipeline template executes."},{"target":"Jaeger (jaeger-collector service)","relation":"JAEGER_COLLECTOR parameter routes API deployment to the collector endpoint at jaeger-collector.d7eovc-dev.svc:14267."},{"target":"PostgreSQL","relation":"Database component deployed as auth-db via postgresql-deploy.json template; test user created manually in pod terminal."},{"target":"OpenShift templates (postgresql-deploy.json, auth-api-pre-deploy.json, auth-api-deploy.json, auth-api-build.json, auth-api-pipeline.json, auth-web-pre-deploy.json, auth-web-deploy.json, auth-web-build.json, auth-web-runtime-build.json, auth-web-pipeline.json)","relation":"Each template is processed with `oc process` and parameters to generate Kubernetes manifests applied to create deployments, builds, and pipelines."}]}
